   },
   "evidence": "At head, src/cli/service.ts:321-322: `const isLoaded = async (unit) => (await ctl([\"print\", `gui/${uid}/${unit.label}`])).exitCode === 0;`. shutdownExecutor (323-340) runs `if (await isLoaded(unit)) { bootout ... }` and then `disable`, so any nonzero print, whatever its cause, skips the bootout and the unload is never checked. The rollback (about lines 902-910) only stops if shutdownExecutor throws, so 'restore previous release' runs next, and recover() (about 382) behaves the same way. The issue requires shutdownExecutor to 'return only when both the unload and the disable are confirmed, and otherwise throw', and says 'If that can't be confirmed, no checkout change happens.' Install's existing `stop` uses the same loose test, but this executor helper is new code written to give the confirmed guarantee."
